  "preamble": "The alveolar trill [r] is realized as the alveolar approximant [ɹ], losing its vibration. In Costa Rican Spanish the trill phoneme (spelled r word-initially and rr between vowels) is widely pronounced [ɹ], a sound described as similar to American English /r/; before a consonant the trill [r] is kept by many speakers.",
